      {
        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on membership tier structure, pricing, and policy constraints.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 54019,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, I've put together the first draft of the membership tiers for T1. The document is here: A1. Please take a look and share your feedback.",
            "mentions": [
              46183,
              52934,
              488135,
              31942
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1",
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 46183,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Thanks. Reading it now. Initial thought on Tier 3 ('Platinum'): the 'unlimited consulting hours' benefit seems risky and could be misinterpreted. We need to define clear boundaries to avoid compliance issues, which is part of T2. I suggest we change it to '10 dedicated consulting hours per month'. It's more concrete and safer.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thinking_face",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 52934,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Good catch, @46183. That aligns with consumer protection best practices. On pricing, the jump from Tier 1 to Tier 2 seems small for the added value. We might cannibalize Tier 2 sales. What if we increase the Tier 2 price by 15% but add one more exclusive feature to justify it?",
            "mentions": [
              46183
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "chart_with_upwards_trend",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 488135,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "The document looks like a good starting point. For the discount rules, are we planning to offer an annual prepayment discount? It's not specified in A1.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 54019,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Yes, we should have a discount. I will add that in.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 46183,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "Let's define it now so it's clear. I propose a standard 10% discount for annual prepayment across all tiers. It's easy to communicate and calculate.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
