      {
        "thread_id": "TH4",
        "thread_goal": "Run pilot, capture feedback, and refine tiers and messaging.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M36",
            "speaker_id": 46183,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, we've completed the first round of pilot calls for T9. I've aggregated the feedback and results in the tracking sheet A4. Key findings:\n1. The value of Tier 2 is not coming across clearly.\n2. We're getting consistent objections on the price of Tier 3.\n3. The objection-handling responses in A3 are working well for common questions.",
            "mentions": [
              52934,
              488135,
              31942,
              54019
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T9",
              "A4",
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bar_chart",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 52934,
            "reply_to": "M36",
            "text": "That matches my experience. I had three calls where the prospect said they didn't see enough of a difference between Tier 1 and Tier 2 to justify the price jump. We need to either add a more compelling benefit to Tier 2 or adjust our messaging in A2 to highlight the value better.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 488135,
            "reply_to": "M36",
            "text": "Same here. The Tier 3 price was a sticking point, but when I used the ROI-focused response from A3, a couple of them became more open to it. The messaging for Tier 2 is definitely the weakest link.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 31942,
            "reply_to": "M36",
            "text": "My calls were difficult. They said it was too expensive.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 46183,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "@31942 Could you add the specific feedback from your calls into the notes column in A4? It's really helpful to capture the exact wording they used.",
            "mentions": [
              31942
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A4"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 54019,
            "reply_to": "M36",
            "text": "One person I talked to was interested in a longer contract term, like two years. Should we add that as an option?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 46183,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "Let's keep things simple for the launch and stick to monthly/annual terms. We can consider longer terms post-launch. Based on the feedback, the most critical change is clarifying the Tier 2 value prop. I propose we refine the messaging in the script A2 to focus on the 'exclusive content library' benefit for Tier 2, as that seemed to resonate most when mentioned.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 52934,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "That's the right move. It's a messaging problem, not a fundamental flaw in the tier structure. Let's double down on explaining the Tier 2 benefits in A2.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 46183,
            "reply_to": "M43",
            "text": "Great. So, for T10, our decision is to adjust the messaging for Tier 2 in the sales script A2 and call outline, but keep the tier structure and pricing in A1 as is for now. This is our decision for D7. @54019, can you own the update to A2?",
            "mentions": [
              54019
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T10",
              "A2",
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D7"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
            "speaker_id": 54019,
            "reply_to": "M44",
            "text": "Yes, I will update the script.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          }
        ],
        "thread_outcome": {
